# Regenerable scrub scratch (naming wave): per-artifact copies of the PRE-rename upstream
# source tree used to prove the dist rewrites were byte-identical after scrubbing. Never a
# deliverable — it carries the very upstream naming this repository purged, 8.8 MB / 1208
# files, and one command regenerates any artifact:
#   node evidence/mpd-naming/wave2/raw/build-repro.mjs <artifact> --apply-scrub --compare
evidence/**/raw/scratch/

# Sandbox WORKING AREAS that lanes create inside their own evidence dir. They hold an isolated
# DSH home, a sandbox HOME, the fixture workspace and a package store — machine-generated
# hundreds of MB that a lane regenerates on every run (measured 2026-09-15: 291 MB / 5308 files
# under evidence/mpd-bridge/dual-path/sandbox alone). The EVIDENCE is REPORT.md + raw/ beside it,
# never this: committing a store snapshot would bloat the repository for no information.
evidence/**/sandbox/

# Packed-tree BUILD PRODUCTS that a lane regenerates on demand. The t70 packer harness writes a FULL
# artifact (18 MB / 1190 files) under its own evidence dir to prove the closure gate against a fresh
# pack without touching the canonical one; what stays committed is the file list + hashes beside it
# (`scratch-artifact-*.files.txt`) and the pinned regeneration command. Same policy as the two rules
# above — measured 2026-09-17.
evidence/**/scratch-artifact*/
evidence/**/scratch-control*/

# REGENERABLE copies of a BUILD PRODUCT inside a lane's evidence. A lane that proves the closure/pack gate
# copies a whole packed tree under `raw/final/` to read it; the artifact itself is gitignored
# (`dist/mpd-package/`), and the copy carries no information that the file list + hashes beside it do not.
# Measured 2026-09-17: 2,410 tracked `raw/final/` paths = 10.68 MB of packed blob bytes, and the whole
# `/raw/` set = 4,582 paths / 28.55 MB, inside a `.git` of 265 MB. Same policy as the three rules above.
# FORWARD-ONLY and deliberate: wave 1 landed with those 2,410 paths ALREADY tracked and they STAY — removing
# them post-merge would mutate the delivered record, and rewriting the commit would dangle the hashes its own
# evidence cites by name (captain's ruling, 2026-09-17). A genuine non-regenerable record that must live at
# this exact path: `git add -f <path>`.
evidence/**/raw/final/

# QA SCRATCH ROOTS at the repository root, ignored BY SHAPE (T-77), not by name. The QA drivers create
# throwaway roots beside the checkout; measured 2026-09-17 in skills/dsh-qa/scripts/**: `.qa-reloc`,
# `.qa-web-client`, `.qa-shipped-path`, and on disk also `.qa-t15-dir`, `.qa-t17-*`, `.qa-t21-dir`,
# `.qa-run-stamp`. The older rules named a few of them individually, so a NEW scratch root was
# machine-generated-but-visible and `git add .` would stage it — the landmine T-77 names. The pattern
# below is root-anchored and family-wide: any top-level `.qa-*` path is scratch, whatever it is called.
# It covers BOTH shapes the drivers actually produce — measured 2026-09-17: directories (`.qa-reloc`,
# `.qa-t15-dir`) and stamp FILES (`.qa-run-stamp`, `.qa-t17-final`, `.qa-before-dir`); a directory-only
# pattern (`/.qa-*/`) left every stamp file visible, which is why the pattern carries no trailing slash.
# It deliberately does NOT match a near-miss that merely shares the prefix without the `.qa-` boundary
# (`/.quarantine-probe`, `/.qaXYZ/`, `qa-scratch/`) — those stay visible, which is the point of a SHAPE
# rather than a longer name list. PREREQUISITE, recorded rather than assumed: the drivers' scratch-root
# CONVENTION is lane D's (plan §4.2); the shape here is DERIVED by measuring the drivers it must cover, and
# it can only ever ignore root paths that already begin `.qa-`.
/.qa-*
